to create a global flag that is
examined by the lexical analyzer, and set by actions.
For example, suppose a program
consists of 0 or more declarations, followed by 0 or more statements.
Consider:
.DS
%{
	int dflag;
%}
  ...  other declarations ...

%%

prog	:	decls  stats
	;

decls	:	/* empty */
			{	dflag = 1;  }
	|	decls  declaration
	;

stats	:	/* empty */
			{	dflag = 0;  }
	|	stats  statement
	;

    ...  other rules ...
.DE
The flag
.I dflag
is now 0 when reading statements, and 1 wh.pn8
